# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots sshd AND nginx - the two services this box exposes
# with no firewall in front of them - and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * both daemons are ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, so verify.sh can
#     hold the agent responsible for keeping them reachable instead of starting
#     them itself (a firewall that blackholes SSH is now a hard FAILURE);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting either daemon cannot kill
#     the container.
#
# Note: the remediation here is kernel netfilter state, not a service config
# file, so there is no "forgot to restart the daemon" variant - but "wrote a ufw
# config without loading any rules into the kernel" is the equivalent mistake and
# verify.sh reads `iptables -S` rather than the config files to catch it.
